A||||13||AkursedX||POLL:  What do you call them?||||5||
Z||000000||AkursedX||11-24-2001||12:20 AM||||This issue came up in my accident thread, and I just figure I would ask....<P>Me?  I call them the Front and Rear Decklids.<P>But if I am getting something from the from the rear storage compartment, I will call the Rear Decklid a "Trunk"<P>This issue has always confused me with mid-engine cars.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||CoolBlue87GT||11-24-2001||12:28 AM||||Front is the bonnet, rear is the hood.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CoolBluesig.gif"> <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000002||Brandon86SE||11-24-2001||12:35 AM||||Front is the hood, rear is the decklid when referring to the engine/ mechanicals, trunk when referring to the trunk.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||TRiAD||11-24-2001||12:39 AM||||...depends on where you live, and who you're talking to...<P><BR>In the US, it's "Hood" for the front, "Decklid" for the rear, and "trunk" if you're talking about it specifically, (ie; I'm going to get _____ out of the trunk now, honey.) ...but you're still opening the decklid to get there...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>If you're in England or Australia, it's "Bonnet" for the front, "Hood" for the rear, "Boot" for the trunk. <BR>I think...<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0RAAAAN8VWdTblRDE93zkbJ*AbWuOFSwE0rtNS2h23KCe3aGgj1O!JDqud!IoFt1NPvdq6rh9ef*226xJh!nSf*vv2Id5gL8WoDCkDX*tCeM/1985-Signature-2.gif">    <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B> ~ Photoshop rendition of planned modifications</I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||soup||11-24-2001||03:21 AM||||rear is boot, front is bonnet...<P>or the thing over the engine, and the thing in the front...<P>they both work||||reg||1
Z||000005||Haze_Performance||11-24-2001||03:39 AM||||Front = Hood<P>Rear = Trunk<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">    <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="purple">Goto Website - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||AusFiero||11-24-2001||06:46 AM||||Yep triad. Bonnet and boot it is.<BR>Except on the Fiero the boot is the bonnet as well  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero4.gif">      <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000007||Cozmo||11-24-2001||08:57 AM||||I gotta agree with Haze...<BR>If it's on the front, it's the hood.<BR>If it's on the rear, it's the trunk.<BR>Doesn't matter what's underneath <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Regionalism does play a large part in nomenclature, tho...<P><P>------------------<BR><B>BobC</B><BR><B>'85 2M6 Targa</B><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/targsig.jpg"> <BR><B>Suncoast Fieros</B>||||reg||10
Z||000008||88CoupeV6||11-24-2001||09:02 AM||||Front is hood <BR>rear is decklid <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||7
Z||000009||Pilrulz||11-24-2001||12:55 PM||||front is hood<BR>rear is decklid, unless referring to trunk<P>pil||||reg||1
Z||000010||LZeitgeist||11-24-2001||01:07 PM||||To avoid confusion, I generally refer to the front as the 'Front', as in "Reach over and pop the front for me, willya?", and I refer to the storage area there as the 'Front Compartment'.<P>For the rear, I always call the rear cover the 'Decklid', and the compartments inside as the 'Engine Compartment' and the 'Back' (or sometimes the 'Trunk').<P>I *think* that in global nomenclature, the front cover is technically called the 'Bonnet' and the rear would be called the 'Boot', but in my (generally United States-specific) experience the term 'Boot' is usually reserved for the area in which a convertable top is stored when folded down, and the cover for this specific area is known as the 'Boot Cover' or 'Tonneau Cover'. <P>Sometimes the flat (not raised like a camper shell) covering over the bed of a pickup truck is also called a 'Tonneau Cover'. <P>O.K., I veered off the subject, but I thought it might be interesting to somebody.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show<P>EDIT - typos<p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 11-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||isthiswhereiputausername?||11-24-2001||01:54 PM||||front trunk/rear trunk  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||FieroMontreal||11-24-2001||02:31 PM||||front = hood<BR>rear = decklid .. sometimes trunk.. depends if I'm talking to someone who knows what a decklid is.... and where the engine in a fiero is located..<P>------------------<BR> -Alex <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontreal_1.gif">   <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> <BR>and Regional Director of CFOG-I for Eastern Canada.||||reg||1
Z||000013||StuGood||11-24-2001||04:40 PM||||True story:  One time a companion and I were taking a cross country trip in my Fiero, and luggage space in back was at a premium.  So I stowed a pair of my boots under the bonnet.  In the front compartment, that is, inside the spare tire (no, she didn't wear bonnets) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.   ||||reg||12
